{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:01:09Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 24, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t# Design: Give tasks a priority\n2\t\n3\tSource: Taiga #4 spec text as provided in this dispatch (see note below).\n4\t\n5\t> **Note on `docs/spec.md`:** at the time of writing, `docs/spec.md` on disk\n6\t> still holds the previous cycle's content (Taiga #3, \"Edit a task title\").\n7\t> The product-manager's Taiga #4 spec was included directly in this\n8\t> dispatch's \"What earlier stages produced\" section, pending the user's\n9\t> confirmation to overwrite `docs/spec.md`/`docs/design.md` and to resolve\n10\t> open question #1 (interleaved vs. full 3-tier sort). This design is built\n11\t> against that inline text, under the same \"interleaved \u2014 only `high`\n12\t> moves\" assumption the spec proceeds under. Recommend the orchestrator\n13\t> confirm both points with the user and persist `docs/spec.md` before the\n14\t> developer stage starts, so the developer isn't working from a stale file\n15\t> on disk.\n16\t\n17\t## Summary of decisions\n18\t\n19\t- **One control does both jobs.** Rather than a read-only badge plus a\n20\t  separate control to change priority (two elements fighting for space in\n21\t  an already-tight row \u2014 see round 2's `Edit`/`Done`/`Delete` row), each\n22\t  task gets a single native `<select>` \u2014 `priority-select` \u2014 that always\n23\t  shows the current priority as its own visible text (\"Low\"/\"Normal\"/\n24\t  \"High\") and lets the user change it in one action. This satisfies AC8\n25\t  (visible at a glance) and the \"control to change priority without\n26\t  entering the title-edit form\" requirement (spec open question 2) with no\n27\t  new UI pattern beyond what the app already has (a styled `<button>`- and\n28\t  `<input>`-adjacent form control).\n29\t- **Color only on the two priorities that deviate from baseline.** `normal`\n30\t  renders with the same neutral border/background every other control in\n31\t  this app uses (`#ccd2d6` border, white fill) \u2014 it's the default, so it\n32\t  shouldn't compete visually. `high` gets a solid warm-orange fill (new\n33\t  accent, not a reuse of `.error`'s red \u2014 see \"Why not reuse the error\n34\t  red\" below). `low` gets a light neutral-gray fill, visually recessive.\n35\t  This means scanning the list, only `high` rows pull the eye, which is\n36\t  literally the ask (\"Let me... see that at a glance\").\n37\t- **Why not reuse the error red (`#a3271d`) for `high`:** round 2's design\n38\t  established the rule \"one red = one meaning\" for this app \u2014 `#a3271d`\n39\t  means \"something is wrong.\" Reusing it for \"high priority\" would make a\n40\t  perfectly valid, successfully-saved task look like an error state.\n41\t  Introducing one new accent (orange, a different hue from red) keeps that\n42\t  semantic separation intact while still giving `high` a color no other\n43\t  element in the app currently uses.\n44\t- **Change applies immediately on select, no separate Save.** Matches this\n45\t  app's two existing precedents for single-field, low-risk actions:\n46\t  `TaskFilter`'s segmented control (click \u2192 immediately re-filters) and the\n47\t  `Done` button (click \u2192 immediately marks complete). A priority change is\n48\t  the same shape of action \u2014 one field, no risk of data loss, no reason to\n49\t  gate it behind a confirm step the way title editing is (title editing\n50\t  needs Save/Cancel because it's multi-character free text where a stray\n51\t  edit is easy to want to undo; a 3-option select isn't).\n52\t- **No optimistic update; follows the existing `run()` pattern exactly.**\n53\t  `App.jsx`'s `run()` helper (lines 33\u201340) awaits the API call, then\n54\t  `refresh()`s from the server, for every existing mutation (add, complete,\n55\t  delete, edit-title). Priority change is wired the same way \u2014 no new\n56\t  state-management pattern introduced. Practical effect: since the\n57\t  `<select>`'s `value` prop is bound to `task.priority` (server state, not\n58\t  local draft state), a failed change causes the control to simply snap\n59\t  back to its last-known-good value on the next render, with the existing\n60\t  global `.error` banner explaining why. No custom revert logic needed \u2014\n61\t  it falls out of the existing controlled-component wiring for free.\n62\t- **Sort is a stable partition applied after the existing filter step**, not\n63\t  a general sort. `high` tasks float to the top in their original relative\n64\t  order; everyone else (interleaved `normal`/`low`) keeps its original\n65\t  relative order below them \u2014 per the spec's explicit \"without disturbing\n66\t  the order of everything else\" and its open-question-1 assumption\n67\t  (interleaved, only `high` moves). JS's `Array.prototype.sort` has been a\n68\t  stable sort in every engine this project targets (Node/V8, all evergreen\n69\t  browsers) since ES2019, so a boolean partition key (`priority === 'high'\n70\t  ? 0 : 1`) is sufficient \u2014 no custom stable-sort implementation needed.\n71\t- **`AddTask` gets the same `priority-select`, defaulted to `normal`.**\n72\t  Reuses the exact same component/class as the row control rather than\n73\t  inventing a second priority-picking pattern for creation vs. editing.\n74\t\n75\t## Component tree change\n76\t\n77\t```\n78\tApp.jsx\n79\t\u251c\u2500 AddTask.jsx\n80\t\u2502   [title input] [priority-select, default \"Normal\"] [Add]   \u2190 select is NEW\n81\t\u251c\u2500 TaskFilter.jsx (unchanged)\n82\t\u2514\u2500 TaskList.jsx\n83\t   \u2514\u2500 <li> per task (TaskRow)\n84\t       [title] [priority-select]  [Edit] [Done] [Delete]      \u2190 select is NEW\n85\t```\n86\t\n87\tNo new files, no new component library. `priority-select` is a shared CSS\n88\tclass (not a new React component) applied to a plain `<select>` in both\n89\t`AddTask.jsx` and `TaskList.jsx`'s `TaskRow`.\n90\t\n91\t## `AddTask.jsx` changes (shape, not full diff)\n92\t\n93\t```jsx\n94\tconst PRIORITIES = [\n95\t  { value: 'low', label: 'Low' },\n96\t  { value: 'normal', label: 'Normal' },\n97\t  { value: 'high', label: 'High' },\n98\t]\n99\t\n100\texport default function AddTask({ onAdd }) {\n101\t  const [title, setTitle] = useState('')\n102\t  const [priority, setPriority] = useState('normal')\n103\t\n104\t  function submit(e) {\n105\t    e.preventDefault()\n106\t    const trimmed = title.trim()\n107\t    if (!trimmed) return\n108\t    onAdd(trimmed, priority)\n109\t    setTitle('')\n110\t    setPriority('normal')\n111\t  }\n112\t\n113\t  return (\n114\t    <form className=\"add-task\" onSubmit={submit}>\n115\t      <input\n116\t        value={title}\n117\t        onChange={(e) => setTitle(e.target.value)}\n118\t        placeholder=\"What needs doing?\"\n119\t        aria-label=\"Task title\"\n120\t      />\n121\t      <select\n122\t        className={`priority-select priority-${priority}`}\n123\t        value={priority}\n124\t        onChange={(e) => setPriority(e.target.value)}\n125\t        aria-label=\"Priority\"\n126\t      >\n127\t        {PRIORITIES.map((p) => <option key={p.value} value={p.value}>{p.label}</option>)}\n128\t      </select>\n129\t      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!title.trim()}>Add</button>\n130\t    </form>\n131\t  )\n132\t}\n133\t```\n134\t\n135\t`PRIORITIES` (value/label pairs) mirrors `TaskFilter.jsx`'s existing\n136\t`OPTIONS` shape exactly \u2014 same pattern, new data.\n137\t\n138\t## `TaskList.jsx` changes (shape, not full diff)\n139\t\n140\tAdd a `priority-select` to `TaskRow`'s **view-mode** row only (edit mode \u2014\n141\tthe title-editing form \u2014 is unaffected; priority stays visible and\n142\teditable independently while a title edit is in progress, matching the\n143\tspec's precedent that title-edit already leaves other fields alone):\n144\t\n145\t```jsx\n146\tconst PRIORITIES = [\n147\t  { value: 'low', label: 'Low' },\n148\t  { value: 'normal', label: 'Normal' },\n149\t  { value: 'high', label: 'High' },\n150\t]\n151\t\n152\t// inside TaskRow(), view-mode return, before the Edit button:\n153\t<select\n154\t  className={`priority-select priority-${task.priority}`}\n155\t  value={task.priority}\n156\t  onChange={(e) => onPriorityChange(task.id, e.target.value)}\n157\t  aria-label={`Priority for ${task.title}`}\n158\t>\n159\t  {PRIORITIES.map((p) => <option key={p.value} value={p.value}>{p.label}</option>)}\n160\t</select>\n161\t```\n162\t\n163\t`onPriorityChange` is a new prop threaded through `TaskList` \u2192\n164\t`TaskRow`, alongside the existing `onComplete`/`onDelete`/`onUpdate`\n165\t(`TaskList.jsx:9`, `:19-21`).\n166\t\n167\t`PRIORITIES` is duplicated between `AddTask.jsx` and `TaskList.jsx` as\n168\twritten above (2 short arrays, 3 entries each) rather than factored into a\n169\tshared constants file \u2014 three lines twice is not worth a new module in a\n170\tproject this size; if a third consumer shows up, that's the point to\n171\tfactor it, not before.\n172\t\n173\t## `api.js` change\n174\t\n175\t```js\n176\texport const setPriority = (id, priority) =>\n177\t  request(`/api/tasks/${id}/priority`, { method: 'PATCH', body: JSON.stringify({ priority }) })\n178\t```\n179\t\n180\tMatches the existing `completeTask`/`updateTask` call shape\n181\t(`api.js:19-21`). `createTask` extends to also send `priority` in its\n182\tbody (exact signature is the developer's call \u2014 mirrors how `updateTask`\n183\talready takes `(id, title)`).\n184\t\n185\t## `App.jsx` changes (shape, not full diff)\n186\t\n187\t```jsx\n188\tconst visibleTasks = tasks.filter((t) => {\n189\t  if (filter === 'open') return !t.done\n190\t  if (filter === 'done') return t.done\n191\t  return true\n192\t})\n193\t\n194\tconst sortedTasks = [...visibleTasks].sort(\n195\t  (a, b) => (a.priority === 'high' ? 0 : 1) - (b.priority === 'high' ? 0 : 1)\n196\t)\n197\t```\n198\t\n199\t`sortedTasks` (not `visibleTasks`) is what gets passed to `<TaskList>`,\n200\tdirectly after the existing filter step (`App.jsx:27-31`) \u2014 sort runs\n201\t*within* the already-filtered subset, satisfying AC7 (a high-priority Done\n202\ttask must not jump into the Open view).\n203\t\n204\t`AddTask`'s `onAdd` callback extends to accept `priority`:\n205\t`onAdd={(title, priority) => run(() => api.createTask(title, priority))}`.\n206\t\n207\t`TaskList` gets a new prop:\n208\t`onPriorityChange={(id, priority) => run(() => api.setPriority(id, priority))}`,\n209\twired identically to the existing `onComplete`/`onDelete`/`onUpdate` props\n210\t(`App.jsx:51-56`).\n211\t\n212\t## `App.css` additions\n213\t\n214\t```css\n215\t.priority-select {\n216\t  padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;\n217\t  border: 1px solid #ccd2d6;\n218\t  border-radius: 5px;\n219\t  background: #fff;\n220\t  color: #16191c;\n221\t  font: inherit;\n222\t  font-size: 0.85rem;\n223\t  cursor: pointer;\n224\t}\n225\t\n226\t.priority-select.priority-high {\n227\t  background: #a8480a;\n228\t  border-color: #a8480a;\n229\t  color: #fff;\n230\t}\n231\t\n232\t.priority-select.priority-low {\n233\t  background: #e8eaec;\n234\t  color: #4a545c;\n235\t}\n236\t\n237\t/* .priority-normal intentionally has no override \u2014 it is the baseline\n238\t   .priority-select styling above, so it blends into the row rather than\n239\t   drawing the eye, same as everything that isn't flagged high. */\n240\t```\n241\t\n242\t`.priority-select` base rule reuses the app's existing border color\n243\t(`#ccd2d6`, already used by `.add-task input` and `.task-title-input`) and\n244\tborder-radius (`5px`, used everywhere else in the file) \u2014 no new geometry\n245\tintroduced. Approximate rendered height with this padding + 1px border +\n246\tdefault line-height \u2248 30\u201332px, in line with the existing `Done`/`Delete`\n247\tbuttons' ~34\u201336px (round 2's design note) \u2014 close enough not to look\n248\tmismatched in the row, and clears the ~24px minimum target size guidance.\n249\t\n250\t## States\n251\t\n252\t### Populated \u2014 the spec's own AC5 example\n253\t\n254\tInput order `[A:normal, B:high, C:low, D:high, E:normal]`, Open filter (or\n255\tAll), rendered order `[B, D, A, C, E]`:\n256\t\n257\t```\n258\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n259\t\u2502 B   [High\u25be]     [Edit][Done][Delete]                       \u2502\n260\t\u2502 D   [High\u25be]     [Edit][Done][Delete]                       \u2502\n261\t\u2502 A   [Normal\u25be]   [Edit][Done][Delete]                       \u2502\n262\t\u2502 C   [Low\u25be]      [Edit][Done][Delete]                       \u2502\n263\t\u2502 E   [Normal\u25be]   [Edit][Done][Delete]                       \u2502\n264\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n265\t```\n266\t`[High\u25be]` renders filled orange (`#a8480a` bg, white text); `[Low\u25be]` a\n267\tlight gray chip (`#e8eaec` bg, `#4a545c` text); `[Normal\u25be]` plain\n268\twhite/bordered, indistinguishable from an ordinary form control. `B` and\n269\t`D` keep their original relative order (`B` before `D`, as in the input);\n270\t`A`, `C`, `E` keep theirs.\n271\t\n272\t### Populated \u2014 no `high` tasks present (AC6)\n273\t\n274\t```\n275\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n276\t\u2502 Buy milk        [Normal\u25be]   [Edit][Done][Delete]            \u2502\n277\t\u2502 Walk the dog     [Low\u25be]     [Edit][Done][Delete]             \u2502\n278\t\u2502 File taxes      [Normal\u25be]   [Edit][Done][Delete]            \u2502\n279\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n280\t```\n281\tOrder is unchanged from today's id order \u2014 the sort key is `0`/`1` on\n282\t\"is this `high`\", so with no `high` present every task ties at `1` and the\n283\tstable sort leaves the array exactly as filtering produced it.\n284\t\n285\t### Populated \u2014 filter interaction (AC7)\n286\t\n287\tGiven the same 5-task set as above but with `B` marked `done`, viewing the\n288\t**Open** filter: `B` (done) is excluded by the existing filter *before*\n289\tthe priority sort runs, so it never appears \u2014 a high-priority Done task\n290\tdoes not pull rows out of order in the Open view:\n291\t\n292\t```\n293\tOpen filter:\n294\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n295\t\u2502 D   [High\u25be]     [Edit][Done][Delete]                       \u2502\n296\t\u2502 A   [Normal\u25be]   [Edit][Done][Delete]                       \u2502\n297\t\u2502 C   [Low\u25be]      [Edit][Done][Delete]                       \u2502\n298\t\u2502 E   [Normal\u25be]   [Edit][Done][Delete]                       \u2502\n299\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n300\t```\n301\t\n302\t### Priority changed (AC9) \u2014 task leaves the top group\n303\t\n304\tBefore (D is `high`, sorted to top) \u2192 user selects \"Normal\" in D's row \u2192\n305\t`onPriorityChange` fires \u2192 `run()` awaits the PATCH, then `refresh()`s \u2192\n306\t`sortedTasks` recomputes on the next render, D falls back to its\n307\tid-ordered position among the non-`high` rows:\n308\t\n309\t```\n310\tBefore:                          After:\n311\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510          \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n312\t\u2502 D  [High\u25be]           \u2502          \u2502 A  [Normal\u25be]         \u2502\n313\t\u2502 A  [Normal\u25be]         \u2502    \u2192     \u2502 C  [Low\u25be]            \u2502\n314\t\u2502 C  [Low\u25be]            \u2502          \u2502 D  [Normal\u25be]         \u2502\n315\t\u2502 E  [Normal\u25be]         \u2502          \u2502 E  [Normal\u25be]         \u2502\n316\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518          \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n317\t```\n318\t\n319\t### Creating a task with an explicit priority (AC2)\n320\t\n321\t```\n322\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n323\t\u2502 [ What needs doing?..............] [High\u25be] [Add]           \u2502\n324\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n325\t```\n326\t`AddTask`'s select defaults to `Normal` (AC1) on mount and resets to\n327\t`Normal` after each successful add \u2014 same reset-after-submit behavior the\n328\ttitle input already has (`setTitle('')`).\n329\t\n330\t### Error \u2014 priority change fails (network/server error)\n331\t\n332\t```\n333\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n334\t\u2502 \u26a0 Could not reach the server.                              \u2502\n335\t\u251c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2524\n336\t\u2502 Buy milk        [Normal\u25be]   [Edit][Done][Delete]            \u2502\n337\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n338\t```\n339\tSame global `.error` banner already used for every other failed mutation\n340\tin this app (unchanged component). The select shows the task's actual\n341\tlast-known-good priority (see \"No optimistic update\" above) rather than\n342\twhatever the user clicked, since it's bound to server state \u2014 no separate\n343\trevert logic to design or build.\n344\t\n345\t### Empty / Loading\n346\t\n347\tUnchanged. `.empty` (per-filter copy) and `.loading` states don't involve\n348\tany task row, so they don't involve priority at all \u2014 no new design\n349\tneeded here.\n350\t\n351\t## Interactive states\n352\t\n353\t- **`priority-select` closed, default (`normal`):** plain bordered control,\n354\t  identical visual weight to `.task-title-input`.\n355\t- **`priority-select` closed, `high`:** solid `#a8480a` fill, white text \u2014\n356\t  the one state in a row designed to actively draw the eye.\n357\t- **`priority-select` closed, `low`:** light `#e8eaec` fill, `#4a545c`\n358\t  text \u2014 visually recessive, consistent with \"low\" meaning \"less urgent\n359\t  than the baseline,\" not \"broken\" or \"hidden.\"\n360\t- **`priority-select` open (dropdown expanded):** native OS/browser\n361\t  rendering for the options list \u2014 not restyled. This app introduces no\n362\t  custom-dropdown component anywhere else, and building one here would be\n363\t  new UI-pattern surface the spec's non-goals don't ask for.\n364\t- **`priority-select` focused:** native browser focus ring, same as every\n365\t  other input/select in this app (no custom `:focus` rule exists\n366\t  anywhere in `App.css` today \u2014 not introducing one here either).\n367\t- **`priority-select` mid-request:** no per-control loading affordance,\n368\t  consistent with round 2's explicit decision that this app has no\n369\t  per-action loading state anywhere (`Done`/`Delete` don't show one\n370\t  either) \u2014 only the shared error banner on failure.\n371\t\n372\t## Accessibility\n373\t\n374\t- **Labels:** `aria-label=\"Priority\"` on `AddTask`'s select,\n375\t  `aria-label={\\`Priority for ${task.title}\\`}` on each row's select \u2014\n376\t  same pattern already used for `Edit`/`Complete`/`Delete`\n377\t  (`TaskList.jsx:74, 89, 91, 95`).\n378\t- **Target size:** `.priority-select`'s padding (`0.4rem 0.6rem` + 1px\n379\t  border) renders at roughly 30\u201332px tall, clearing the ~24px minimum and\n380\t  sitting close to the row's existing `Edit`/`Done`/`Delete` buttons\n381\t  (~34\u201336px per round 2's note) so it doesn't look like a stray smaller\n382\t  control.\n383\t- **Keyboard:** native `<select>` \u2014 full keyboard support (arrow keys to\n384\t  change value, Enter/Space to open, no custom key handling needed). Tab\n385\t  order in a row becomes `priority-select \u2192 Edit \u2192 Done \u2192 Delete`, visual\n386\t  left-to-right, no `tabIndex` overrides, matching this app's existing \"no\n387\t  tab-order overrides anywhere\" pattern.\n388\t- **Color is not the only signal:** every state also shows its label text\n389\t  (\"Low\"/\"Normal\"/\"High\") inside the control itself \u2014 color reinforces,\n390\t  it doesn't carry the meaning alone. Satisfies WCAG 1.4.1 (use of color).\n391\t- **Contrast \u2014 computed, not assumed:**\n392\t\n393\t  **`high`: white text `#ffffff` on `#a8480a` fill.**\n394\t  - `#a8480a` \u2192 sRGB (0.6588, 0.2824, 0.0392)\n395\t  - linearized: R \u2248 0.3914, G \u2248 0.0648, B \u2248 0.003035\n396\t  - L = 0.2126\u00d70.3914 + 0.7152\u00d70.0648 + 0.0722\u00d70.003035 \u2248 0.1298\n397\t  - white L = 1.0\n398\t  - contrast = (1.0 + 0.05) / (0.1298 + 0.05) \u2248 **5.84:1** \u2014 passes the\n399\t    4.5:1 text minimum with real margin (this is a first-pass color; an\n400\t    earlier candidate, `#c2540d`, computed to 4.60:1 \u2014 too close to the\n401\t    line for comfort, so I darkened it to `#a8480a` for headroom).\n402\t  - Same figure covers the `border-color` (set equal to the fill) against\n403\t    the white `.task` card background for the 3:1 non-text minimum \u2014 5.84\n404\t    clears it easily.\n405\t\n406\t  **`low`: text `#4a545c` on `#e8eaec` fill.**\n407\t  - `#e8eaec` (bg) \u2192 linearized R \u2248 0.8071, G \u2248 0.8228, B \u2248 0.8389 \u2192\n408\t    L \u2248 0.8206\n409\t  - `#4a545c` (text) \u2192 linearized R \u2248 0.0684, G \u2248 0.0886, B \u2248 0.1072 \u2192\n410\t    L \u2248 0.0857\n411\t  - contrast = (0.8206 + 0.05) / (0.0857 + 0.05) \u2248 **6.42:1** \u2014 passes\n412\t    with margin.\n413\t  - Contrast of the `#e8eaec` fill itself against the white `.task` card\n414\t    background is only \u2248 **1.21:1** (L 0.8206 vs 1.0) \u2014 far under the 3:1\n415\t    non-text minimum, meaning the chip's fill alone wouldn't read as a\n416\t    distinct shape against a white card. That's why `.priority-select`'s\n417\t    base rule already carries a `1px solid #ccd2d6` border \u2014 for `low`\n418\t    this border isn't overridden, so it inherits that same border (already\n419\t    \u22653:1 by existing precedent elsewhere in the file) and the chip stays\n420\t    visually distinct by its outline even though the fill alone would not\n421\t    be.\n422\t  - `normal` needs no computation \u2014 it's the unmodified base style, already\n423\t    in production use.\n424\t\n425\t## Acceptance criteria traceability\n426\t\n427\t| AC | Design element |\n428\t|----|-----------------|\n429\t| 1 | `AddTask`'s `priority-select` defaults to `normal` on mount/reset |\n430\t| 2 | `priority-select` in `AddTask`, value sent via `onAdd(title, priority)` \u2192 `api.createTask` |\n431\t| 3 | Row's `priority-select` `onChange` \u2192 `onPriorityChange(task.id, value)` \u2192 `api.setPriority`, only priority sent, mirrors title-edit precedent of touching one field |\n432\t| 4 | Select only ever offers the 3 valid `<option>`s \u2014 invalid values aren't reachable via this UI; 422 is a backend defense-in-depth case (same precedent as title-edit's AC8) |\n433\t| 5 | `sortedTasks` stable partition in `App.jsx`, applied after `visibleTasks`; \"Populated \u2014 AC5 example\" wireframe |\n434\t| 6 | Partition key ties (`1`/`1`) when no `high` present \u2192 stable sort is a no-op; \"no `high` tasks\" wireframe |\n435\t| 7 | Sort applied to `visibleTasks` (post-filter), not raw `tasks`; \"filter interaction\" wireframe |\n436\t| 8 | `priority-select` always shows current value as visible text + color, no edit-mode required |\n437\t| 9 | Sort recomputes on every render from `task.priority`; \"priority changed\" before/after wireframe |\n438\t| 10 | Priority `<select>` and title-edit form are fully independent controls/state \u2014 editing one never touches the other, same as `done` already being independent of title today |\n439\t\n440\t## Non-goals honored\n441\t\n442\tNo new sort/filter UI control \u2014 the priority sort is automatic, exactly as\n443\tscoped. No priority levels beyond low/normal/high \u2014 the `PRIORITIES` array\n444\thas exactly 3 entries. No bulk editing \u2014 each row's select is independent,\n445\tsame as every other per-row control in this app. No change to `done`\n446\tfiltering/sorting \u2014 the sort step runs strictly after the existing filter,\n447\ttouches nothing about how `done` is computed or displayed. No priority\n448\thistory/audit trail \u2014 the select shows current value only, nothing new\n449\tpersisted about past values. No new UI library, icon set, or token\n450\tsystem \u2014 one new CSS class family (`priority-select` + two modifiers)\n451\tusing colors and geometry already established or freshly computed and\n452\tjustified above, no external dependency added.\n453\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01FcC7otW3GYW4U5pfrYNDEL", "session_id": "7f5e0a1a-3392-4c0e-af12-a01e18a479a1"}}
