{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:02:05Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 69, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t\"\"\"Route wiring only -- behaviour lives in store.py.\"\"\"\n2\tfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\n3\tfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\n4\t\n5\tfrom .models import PriorityIn, Task, TaskIn\n6\tfrom .store import store\n7\t\n8\tapp = FastAPI(title=\"test-project\")\n9\t\n10\t# A regex, not a fixed list: the dev server is reached as both localhost and\n11\t# 127.0.0.1, and the e2e harness binds it to a free port rather than 5173, so\n12\t# a hardcoded origin silently blocks every write from the browser while GETs\n13\t# keep working -- which reads as \"adding a task does nothing\".\n14\tapp.add_middleware(\n15\t    CORSMiddleware,\n16\t    allow_origin_regex=r\"http://(localhost|127\\.0\\.0\\.1):\\d+\",\n17\t    allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n18\t    allow_headers=[\"*\"],\n19\t)\n20\t\n21\t\n22\t@app.get(\"/api/tasks\", response_model=list[Task])\n23\tdef list_tasks() -> list[Task]:\n24\t    return store.list()\n25\t\n26\t\n27\t@app.post(\"/api/tasks\", response_model=Task, status_code=201)\n28\tdef create_task(payload: TaskIn) -> Task:\n29\t    return store.add(payload.title, payload.priority)\n30\t\n31\t\n32\t@app.post(\"/api/tasks/{task_id}/done\", response_model=Task)\n33\tdef complete_task(task_id: int) -> Task:\n34\t    task = store.set_done(task_id, True)\n35\t    if task is None:\n36\t        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"no such task\")\n37\t    return task\n38\t\n39\t\n40\t@app.patch(\"/api/tasks/{task_id}/priority\", response_model=Task)\n41\tdef update_priority(task_id: int, payload: PriorityIn) -> Task:\n42\t    task = store.set_priority(task_id, payload.priority)\n43\t    if task is None:\n44\t        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"no such task\")\n45\t    return task\n46\t\n47\t\n48\t@app.patch(\"/api/tasks/{task_id}\", response_model=Task)\n49\tdef update_task(task_id: int, payload: TaskIn) -> Task:\n50\t    task = store.update_title(task_id, payload.title)\n51\t    if task is None:\n52\t        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"no such task\")\n53\t    return task\n54\t\n55\t\n56\t@app.delete(\"/api/tasks/{task_id}\", status_code=204)\n57\tdef delete_task(task_id: int) -> None:\n58\t    if not store.delete(task_id):\n59\t        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"no such task\")\n60\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01UFh35x8oYLkVpYk4egEj44", "session_id": "7f5e0a1a-3392-4c0e-af12-a01e18a479a1"}}
{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:02:14Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 70, "kind": "message", "text": "This matches the design (`PATCH /api/tasks/{id}/priority` per `docs/design.md:176-178`). Backend implementation is complete and verified.\n\n## Backend handoff summary\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `backend/app/models.py` \u2014 added `Priority = Literal[\"low\", \"normal\", \"high\"]`; `TaskIn` and `Task` gained `priority: Priority = \"normal\"`; added `PriorityIn` (single-field model for the priority-update endpoint). Invalid values are rejected with `422` automatically via Pydantic's `Literal` validation \u2014 no manual check needed.\n- `backend/app/store.py` \u2014 `TaskStore.add()` takes an optional `priority` (default `\"normal\"`); added `set_priority()` mirroring the existing `set_done()` shape.\n- `backend/app/main.py` \u2014 `create_task` passes `payload.priority` through; added `PATCH /api/tasks/{task_id}/priority` (matches `docs/design.md`'s `api.js` contract \u2014 note this uses `PATCH`, not `POST` like `/done`, since that's what the design doc's frontend call already specifies).\n- `backend/tests/test_tasks.py` \u2014 8 new tests: default priority on create, explicit priority on create, invalid priority rejected on create (no mutation), priority update, priority update leaves title/id/done untouched, 404 on missing task, invalid priority rejected on update (no mutation), title update leaves priority untouched.\n\n**Verification:** `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 22 passed (14 pre-existing + 8 new). Two pre-existing, unrelated warnings (httpx2 deprecation notice, pytest cache write permission).\n\n**Deviation from spec draft:** the inline spec said \"mirrors the existing `/done` action-scoped route\" (implying `POST`), but `docs/design.md`'s frontend `api.js` snippet explicitly calls `PATCH .../priority`. I followed the design doc since it's the more concrete, later-stage artifact \u2014 flagging in case that was an unintentional mismatch between stages.\n\n**Known gap:** `docs/spec.md` on disk still holds the prior cycle's content (per both earlier stages' notes) \u2014 I did not touch it, since resolving that overwrite was called out as needing user confirmation first.\n\nFrontend scope (api.js, AddTask.jsx, TaskList.jsx, App.jsx, App.css) is out of my scope and untouched.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "7f5e0a1a-3392-4c0e-af12-a01e18a479a1"}}
